🚀 Frontend Deployment Documentation

This document explains the step-by-step process to deploy the frontend application on the server using SSH, Git, Bun, and PM2.

🔐 Server Access

1. Connect to the server via SSH:

ssh root@<SERVER_IP>

---------------------------------------------------
  
2. Enter:

Username

Password

---------------------------------------------------

📁 Navigate to Project Directory

3. List files to verify location:

ls

---------------------------------------------------

4. Move to the required directory:

cd <project-folder>

---------------------------------------------------

5. Navigate to the correct frontend project:

cd <frontend-project-name>

---------------------------------------------------

🔄 Pull Latest Code from Git

Pull latest changes:

6. git pull

---------------------------------------------------

7. If prompted, enter:

Git username

Git password / Personal Access Token

---------------------------------------------------

🏷️ Checkout Specific Version (Tag)

8. Fetch all branches and tags (recommended):

git fetch --all --tags

---------------------------------------------------
  
9. Checkout the required version:

git checkout origin/v0.0.3

---------------------------------------------------


10. Switch to the tag:

git checkout v0.0.3

---------------------------------------------------

11. Verify the current version:

git status

---------------------------------------------------

📦 Install Dependencies (Bun)

12. Ensure Bun is installed:

bun --version

---------------------------------------------------


13. Install dependencies:

bun install

---------------------------------------------------

🏗️ Build the Project

14. Build the frontend:

bun run build

---------------------------------------------------

⚙️ PM2 Process Management

15. List running PM2 processes:

pm2 ls

---------------------------------------------------

16. Restart the frontend service
(example: PM2 process ID = 13)

pm2 restart 13

---------------------------------------------------
  
17. Save PM2 process state:

pm2 save
